 Full-text search runs in the database, not Elasticsearch. On MySQL it is sharded 16 ways by CRC32 of the account ID (`Search::Record::Trilogy`); on SQLite it is a single FTS5 index (`Search::Record::SQLite`). Don't assume the sharded shape when working under SQLite. Models in `app/models/search/`.
 
+### Languages
+
+Fizzy is translated into English (default) and Japanese. `config/locales/en.yml` and
+`config/locales/ja.yml` mirror each other key for key. Views use lazy lookups (`t(".key")`), other
+Ruby uses full keys, and JavaScript reads the strings it needs from the `translations` meta tag.
+`?locale=ja` switches language and is remembered in the session and on the `Identity`. See
+"Languages" in `docs/development.md`.
+
